  note      = {CORE ARGUMENT: Knowles provides a textbook guide to the Philosophy of Right that situates Hegel's arguments against their Kantian and Rousseauian backgrounds, showing how Hegel's critique of abstract right and morality responds directly to Kant's formalism and Rousseau's voluntarism. RELEVANCE: The background chapters on Kant and Rousseau are useful for establishing which elements Hegel accepts, modifies, and rejects; accessible reference for tracking source-transformations. POSITION: Non-metaphysical, analytically oriented presentation.},
  keywords  = {hegel-kant, hegel-rousseau, philosophy-of-right, guide, Medium}
